{"main":"\n<div id=\"ROOT\" style=\"font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #222; max-width: 1240px; background: #fff; padding: 6px\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:14px; align-items:center\">\n    <label><b>T</b> <input type=\"range\" id=\"ROOT-T\" min=\"0\" max=\"2000\" step=\"1\" style=\"width:430px; vertical-align:middle\"></label>\n    <span id=\"ROOT-Tv\" style=\"min-width:90px; font-weight:bold\"></span>\n    <label>target <select id=\"ROOT-tg\"></select></label>\n    <label title=\"Compound elastic from a Hauser–Feshbach (TALYS) calculation with the same potential; the slider moves only within its calculated range\">compound elastic, within the calculated range: lower <input type=\"range\" id=\"ROOT-c\" min=\"0\" max=\"1\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"1\" style=\"width:110px; vertical-align:middle\"> upper</label>\n    <span id=\"ROOT-cv\"></span>\n    <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ROOT-bl\"> black sphere</label>\n    <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ROOT-hs\"> billiard balls</label>\n    <label>Difference y range <select id=\"ROOT-diff-scale\"><option value=\"0\">configured (±0.25 b/sr by default)</option><option value=\"0.05\">±0.05 b/sr</option><option value=\"0.1\">±0.1 b/sr</option><option value=\"0.25\">±0.25 b/sr</option><option value=\"1\">±1 b/sr</option><option value=\"5\">±5 b/sr</option><option value=\"20\">±20 b/sr</option></select></label>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"ROOT-libraries\" style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:8px 0\"></div>\n  <div id=\"ROOT-pre\" style=\"margin:6px 0\"></div>\n  <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap:6px\">\n    <canvas id=\"ROOT-a\"></canvas><canvas id=\"ROOT-b\"></canvas><canvas id=\"ROOT-c2\"></canvas><canvas id=\"ROOT-d\"></canvas>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap:6px\">\n    <canvas id=\"ROOT-diff\" aria-label=\"ENDF/B-VII.1 minus JENDL-4.0u elastic differential cross section\"></canvas>\n    <div style=\"padding:20px;line-height:1.6\"><b>Is ENDF minus JENDL approximately constant?</b>\n      <p>Purple is \\(\\Delta(\\mu) = (d\\sigma/d\\Omega)_{\\text{ENDF/B-VII.1}} - (d\\sigma/d\\Omega)_{\\text{JENDL-4.0u}}\\), in b/sr, against \\(\\mu = \\cos\\theta\\) (CM), with forward scattering (\\(\\mu = 1\\)) at the left as in the other plots; the top scale gives \\(\\theta\\). Positive means ENDF is higher; negative means JENDL is higher.</p>\n      <p>Against \\(\\mu\\), equal widths are equal solid angle (\\(d\\Omega = 2\\pi\\, d\\mu\\)): a constant difference (Legendre order \\(L = 0\\)) is a flat line, a \\(\\cos\\theta\\) term (\\(L = 1\\)) a straight line, and \\(2\\pi\\) times the signed area under the curve is \\(\\sigma_{\\text{el,ENDF}} - \\sigma_{\\text{el,JENDL}}\\). The black dashed line is \\(C = (\\sigma_{\\text{el,ENDF}} - \\sigma_{\\text{el,JENDL}})/4\\pi\\), the constant with that area.</p>\n      <p>At 2.45 MeV the difference is neither constant nor a cos θ term: ENDF is lower at forward angles and higher over most larger angles, by an amount that varies. A sign change rules out explaining the whole difference by a positive isotropic term. The comparison does not use the model or the compound slider.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"ROOT-diff-info\" style=\"margin:4px 0;line-height:1.45\"></div>\n  <div id=\"ROOT-info\" style=\"margin:4px 0 8px 0; line-height:1.45\"></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin:4px 0\"><b>Elastic angular/recoil plots only.</b> Total = elastic + non-elastic. Non-elastic includes inelastic, capture and other open channels; their individual spectra are not calculated here.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin:4px 0\"><b>Model:</b> shape elastic from the spherical Koning–Delaroche potential, plus compound elastic from a Hauser–Feshbach (TALYS) calculation with the same potential, with its calculated angular shape. The slider moves only within that calculation's range with a width-fluctuation correction. Compound elastic moves cross section from non-elastic to elastic, so the <b>total stays fixed</b>; the evaluated libraries are never changed.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin:4px 0\"><b>Model curves:</b> blue solid = shape elastic; orange dashed = shape + compound elastic; orange dotted = compound elastic alone. The model is one potential; it does not tell which evaluation is right.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin:4px 0\"><b>Plot ranges:</b> angular y = 0.001–20 b/sr; recoil x = 0–1.15 × E_max (mean Xe), matching the plotted endpoint marker; the recoil plot's top scale gives \\((1-\\cos\\theta)/2 = E_r/E_{\\max}\\), exact for one isotope and for the mean-mass endpoint with natural xenon. Recoil x follows energy/target changes; compound and library controls leave the axes fixed. These fixed y ranges are shared by the portable notebook and website.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin:4px 0\">Evaluated curves interpolate a teaching grid. Deep minima between energy samples can differ substantially from the source. Exact 2.45 and 14.1 MeV samples are included; angles use 1° spacing. Unreconstructed resonance ranges are masked.</div>\n</div>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var D = __DATA__;\n  var HBARC = 197.3269804, MN = 939.56542, AMU = 931.49410, ZXE = 54;\n  function f32(b64) { var s = atob(b64), n = s.length, u = new Uint8Array(n); for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) u[i] = s.charCodeAt(i); return new Float32Array(u.buffer); }\n  var T = D.Tvalues, TH = f32(D.th), DS = f32(D.dsdo), EL = f32(D.el), RE = f32(D.re), TOT = f32(D.tot), ELL = f32(D.el_l), REL = f32(D.re_l);\n  var nT = D.nT, nA = D.nA, nTh = D.nTh, nL = D.nL, A = D.A;\n  var LIB = D.libraries || {};\n  Object.keys(LIB).forEach(function(key) { var b = LIB[key]; b.dsdo = f32(b.dsdo); b.el = f32(b.el); b.tot = f32(b.tot); });\n  var CP = D.compound || null;   // compound elastic from TALYS (talys_compound.py)\n  if (CP) { CP.lo = f32(CP.lo); CP.hi = f32(CP.hi); CP.def = f32(CP.default); CP.reac = f32(CP.reaction); CP.shape = f32(CP.shape);\n    CP.logT = CP.T.map(Math.log); CP.nTh = CP.theta.length; }\n  function compoundAt(t, s) {   // port of talys_compound.at()\n    var lt = Math.log(t), n = CP.T.length, i = 0; while (i < n - 2 && CP.logT[i + 1] < lt) i++;\n    var f = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (lt - CP.logT[i]) / (CP.logT[i + 1] - CP.logT[i])));\n    var res = {sigma: [], lo: [], hi: [], def: [], reac: [], shape: []};\n    for (var j = 0; j < nA; j++) { var a = i * nA + j, b = (i + 1) * nA + j;\n      var lo = (1 - f) * CP.lo[a] + f * CP.lo[b], hi = (1 - f) * CP.hi[a] + f * CP.hi[b];\n      res.lo.push(lo); res.hi.push(hi); res.sigma.push(lo + s * (hi - lo));\n      res.def.push((1 - f) * CP.def[a] + f * CP.def[b]); res.reac.push((1 - f) * CP.reac[a] + f * CP.reac[b]);\n      var row = new Float64Array(CP.nTh), a0 = a * CP.nTh, b0 = b * CP.nTh;\n      for (var k = 0; k < CP.nTh; k++) row[k] = (1 - f) * CP.shape[a0 + k] + f * CP.shape[b0 + k];\n      res.shape.push(row); }\n    return res; }\n  var LOGD = new Float32Array(DS.length); for (var q = 0; q < DS.length; q++) LOGD[q] = Math.log(Math.max(DS[q], 1e-30));\n  var LOGT = new Float64Array(nT); for (q = 0; q < nT; q++) LOGT[q] = Math.log(T[q]);\n  var COS = new Float64Array(nTh); for (q = 0; q < nTh; q++) COS[q] = Math.cos(TH[q] * Math.PI / 180);\n  var C = {om: \"#1f77b4\", omComp: \"#e66101\", ce: \"#ff7f0e\", black: \"#404040\", hard: \"#8c8c8c\", dip: \"#d62728\", wd: \"#2ca02c\"};\n  var el = function (id) { return document.getElementById(\"ROOT-\" + id); };\n\n  function kin(t, a) { var M = a * AMU, mu = MN * M / (MN + M), ecm = t * M / (MN + M);\n    return {k: Math.sqrt(2 * mu * ecm) / HBARC, emax: 4 * MN * M / ((MN + M) * (MN + M)) * t * 1e3}; }\n  function kd(a, e) { var asym = (a - 2 * ZXE) / a, a13 = Math.pow(a, 1 / 3), f = e - (-11.2814 + 0.02646 * a);\n    var v1 = 59.30 - 21.0 * asym - 0.024 * a, v2 = 0.007228 - 1.48e-6 * a, v3 = 1.994e-5 - 2.0e-8 * a, v4 = 7.0e-9;\n    var w1 = 12.195 + 0.0167 * a, w2 = 73.55 + 0.0795 * a;\n    var d1 = 16.0 - 16.0 * asym, d2 = 0.0180 + 0.003802 / (1 + Math.exp((a - 156.0) / 8.0)), d3 = 11.5;\n    return {VV: v1 * (1 - v2 * f + v3 * f * f - v4 * f * f * f), WV: w1 * f * f / (f * f + w2 * w2),\n            WD: d1 * f * f * Math.exp(-d2 * f) / (f * f + d3 * d3),\n            RV: (1.3039 - 0.4054 / a13) * a13, aV: 0.6778 - 1.487e-4 * a, RD: (1.3424 - 0.01585 * a13) * a13, aD: 0.5446 - 1.656e-4 * a}; }\n  function interp(x, xs, ys) { // xs ascending, linear, clamped\n    var n = xs.length; if (x <= xs[0]) return ys[0]; if (x >= xs[n - 1]) return ys[n - 1];\n    var lo = 0, hi = n - 1; while (hi - lo > 1) { var mid = (lo + hi) >> 1; if (xs[mid] <= x) lo = mid; else hi = mid; }\n    var t = (x - xs[lo]) / (xs[hi] - xs[lo]); return ys[lo] + t * (ys[hi] - ys[lo]); }\n\n  function frame(t, wts, comp) {   // port of diffraction_grid.frame()\n    var lt = Math.log(t), i = 0; while (i < nT - 2 && LOGT[i + 1] <= lt) i++;\n    var f = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (lt - LOGT[i]) / (LOGT[i + 1] - LOGT[i])));\n    var ws = 0, j, m; for (j = 0; j < nA; j++) ws += wts[j];\n    var w = wts.map(function (v) { return v / ws; });\n    var lin = function (arr, jj) { return (1 - f) * arr[i * nA + jj] + f * arr[(i + 1) * nA + jj]; };\n    var logDj = [], reI = [], elI = [], totI = [], E = [], eHi = 0, eLo = 1e99, aMean = 0;\n    for (j = 0; j < nA; j++) {\n      var row = new Float64Array(nTh), b0 = (i * nA + j) * nTh, b1 = ((i + 1) * nA + j) * nTh;\n      for (m = 0; m < nTh; m++) row[m] = (1 - f) * LOGD[b0 + m] + f * LOGD[b1 + m];\n      logDj.push(row); reI.push(lin(RE, j)); elI.push(lin(EL, j)); totI.push(lin(TOT, j));\n      E.push(kin(t, A[j]).emax); aMean += w[j] * A[j];\n      if (w[j] > 0) { eHi = Math.max(eHi, E[j]); eLo = Math.min(eLo, E[j]); }\n    }\n    var cs = (comp !== null && comp !== undefined && CP) ? compoundAt(t, comp) : null;\n    var dsdoComp = new Float64Array(nTh);\n    if (cs) for (j = 0; j < nA; j++) if (w[j] > 0) for (m = 0; m < nTh; m++) dsdoComp[m] += w[j] * cs.sigma[j] / (4 * Math.PI) * interp(TH[m], CP.theta, cs.shape[j]);\n    var dsdo = new Float64Array(nTh), dsdoShape = new Float64Array(nTh);\n    for (m = 0; m < nTh; m++) { var s = 0; for (j = 0; j < nA; j++) if (w[j] > 0) s += w[j] * Math.exp(logDj[j][m]); dsdoShape[m] = s; dsdo[m] = s + dsdoComp[m]; }\n    var nE = 400, er = new Float64Array(nE), dsde = new Float64Array(nE), dsdeShape = new Float64Array(nE);\n    for (m = 0; m < nE; m++) er[m] = eHi * m / (nE - 1);\n    for (j = 0; j < nA; j++) { if (!(w[j] > 0)) continue;\n      for (m = 0; m < nE; m++) { if (er[m] > E[j] * (1 + 1e-12)) continue;\n        var ang = Math.acos(Math.min(1, Math.max(-1, 1 - 2 * er[m] / E[j]))) * 180 / Math.PI;\n        var shape = 4 * Math.PI / E[j] * Math.exp(interp(ang, TH, logDj[j]));\n        dsdeShape[m] += w[j] * shape;\n        dsde[m] += w[j] * (shape + (cs ? cs.sigma[j] / E[j] * interp(ang, CP.theta, cs.shape[j]) : 0)); } }\n    var km = kin(t, aMean), p = kd(aMean, t), R = p.RV, k = km.k, eMean = km.emax, L = Math.floor(k * R);\n    var black = new Float64Array(nTh);\n    for (m = 0; m < nTh; m++) { var x = COS[m], Pp = 1, P = x, amp = 1; if (L >= 1) amp += 3 * x;\n      for (var l = 1; l < L; l++) { var Pn = ((2 * l + 1) * x * P - l * Pp) / (l + 1); Pp = P; P = Pn; amp += (2 * l + 3) * P; }\n      black[m] = Math.pow(amp / (2 * k), 2) / 100; }\n    var hard = R * R / 400, dsdeB = new Float64Array(nE), dsdeH = new Float64Array(nE);\n    for (m = 0; m < nE; m++) { if (er[m] > eMean * (1 + 1e-12)) continue;\n      var a2 = Math.acos(Math.min(1, Math.max(-1, 1 - 2 * er[m] / eMean))) * 180 / Math.PI;\n      dsdeB[m] = 4 * Math.PI / eMean * interp(a2, TH, black); dsdeH[m] = 4 * Math.PI / eMean * hard; }\n    var dips = [];\n    for (m = 1; m < nE - 1; m++) if (er[m] > 0.03 * eLo && er[m] < 0.97 * eLo && er[m - 1] > 0.03 * eLo && er[m + 1] < 0.97 * eLo\n        && dsde[m] < dsde[m - 1] && dsde[m] <= dsde[m + 1]) dips.push(er[m]);\n    var elL = new Float64Array(nL), reL = new Float64Array(nL);\n    for (var ll = 0; ll < nL; ll++) for (j = 0; j < nA; j++) {\n      elL[ll] += w[j] * ((1 - f) * ELL[(i * nA + j) * nL + ll] + f * ELL[((i + 1) * nA + j) * nL + ll]);\n      reL[ll] += w[j] * ((1 - f) * REL[(i * nA + j) * nL + ll] + f * REL[((i + 1) * nA + j) * nL + ll]); }\n    var sum = function (arr) { var s2 = 0; for (var jj = 0; jj < nA; jj++) s2 += w[jj] * arr[jj]; return s2; };\n    var evaluated = libraryFrame(t, w, er);\n    var wsum = function (arr) { var s3 = 0; for (var jj = 0; jj < nA; jj++) s3 += w[jj] * arr[jj]; return s3; };\n    var compound = cs ? {sigma: wsum(cs.sigma), lo: wsum(cs.lo), hi: wsum(cs.hi), def: wsum(cs.def), reaction: wsum(cs.reac)} : null;\n    return {libraries: evaluated, difference: libraryDifference(evaluated), dsdo: dsdo, dsdoShape: dsdoShape, dsdeShape: dsdeShape, dsdoComp: dsdoComp, compound: compound,\n            black: black, hard: hard, er: er, dsde: dsde, dsdeB: dsdeB, dsdeH: dsdeH, dips: dips, eMean: eMean,\n            eLo: eLo, eHi: eHi, k: k, R: R, kR: k * R, el: sum(elI), re: sum(reI), tot: sum(totI), elL: elL, reL: reL, p: p};\n  }\n\n  function libraryFrame(t, w, er) { // port of evaluated_libraries.frame()\n    var active=[], answer={};\n    for(var j=0;j<nA;j++) if(w[j]>0) active.push(j);\n    Object.keys(LIB).forEach(function(key) {\n      var b=LIB[key], ts=b.T, i=0; while(i<ts.length-2 && ts[i+1]<=t) i++;\n      var f=(t-ts[i])/(ts[i+1]-ts[i]), needed=f===0?[i]:f===1?[i+1]:[i,i+1];\n      var good=t>=ts[0] && t<=ts[ts.length-1] && needed.every(function(q) {\n        return active.every(function(j) {return !!b.valid[q*nA+j];});});\n      var result={label:b.label,color:b.color,available:good}; answer[key]=result;\n      if(!good) {var missing=active.some(function(j){return b.bounds[j][0]===null;});\n        var lo=0,hi=Infinity; active.forEach(function(j){lo=Math.max(lo,b.bounds[j][0]);hi=Math.min(hi,b.bounds[